In addition to Andy's point, the derivation of CI's for abundance is not always straightforward, given the distribution of N -- especially if the CI is based on the likelihood profile. As a quick intro to *some* of the issues, this is presented in the MARK book, chapter 14 (in particular, section 14.10.1, and the - sidebar - on p. 14, which actually shows that for some models, there is no upper bound for the likelihood profile, meaning the upper bound for any CI is infinite.

