Hello group,

I searched the previous posts and couldn't find anything on this.
I ran the same models in Presence and Unmarked.
The models have the same AIC and comparable parameter estimates for PSI
but the SEs for unmarked are consistently  larger in unmarked (see example below)

I would greatly appreciate any thoughts on the matter

Presence output

Number of parameters           = 3
Number of function calls           = 76
-2log(likelihood)              = 93.1348
AIC                            = 99.1348
LikeNRSig=6 eps=0.01 ETA=1e-013

Untransformed Estimates of coefficients for covariates (Beta's)
======================================================================
                                          estimate    std.error
A1   psi                              :  -3.874362    1.557832
A2   psi.VegHt                        :   0.049314    0.026646
B1   P[1]                             :   0.630795    0.301144

============================================================

unmarked output

Occupancy (logit-scale):
            Estimate     SE     z P(>|z|)
(Intercept)  -3.8698 2.0046 -1.93  0.0536
veght         0.0492 0.0343  1.44  0.1509

Detection (logit-scale):
 Estimate    SE   z P(>|z|)
    0.631 0.301 2.1  0.0362

AIC: 99.13486
Number of sites: 29
optim convergence code: 0
optim iterations: 24
Bootstrap iterations: 0

